  howpublished = {IEEE Sensors Journal},
  annotation = {中文辅助译名：基于数字忆阻器的神经网络用于电子鼻中的气体识别},
  abstract = {The electronic nose (e-nose) is widely used in environmental monitoring, product quality control, and medical diagnostics. Deep learning has greatly improved pattern recognition, but high-performance neural networks often require many parameters. Traditional computing architectures, which involve frequent data transmission and storage, are inefficient and consume a lot of energy, making them unsuitable for rapid-response e-nose applications like on-site detection or mobile devices. Memristors, which combine storage and computation in one device, offer a solution by reducing power consumption and increasing efficiency. However, real memristor chips and large-scale arrays are still hard to obtain. Therefore, this paper proposes an efficient digital memristor neuron circuit design based on Field-Programmable Gate Array (FPGA). Additionally, we introduce a resource-efficient digital memristor array design scheme to maximize the implementation of digital memristor array with limited resources. We also develop a gas data acquisition system that utilizes sensor arrays for data collection and performs two-dimensional processing on the data. To achieve gas recognition, we present a lightweight mixed-precision quantized convolutional neural network (LHPQ-CNN). We successfully deployed the LHPQ-CNN model on an FPGA-based digital memristor array, resulting in the creation of an advanced e-nose pattern recognition system. Our experimental results demonstrate an impressive accuracy rate of},
}

